# What the api image build must never take from a checkout. Docker sends the
# build context (this directory) minus every path matched here, and the
# Dockerfile's `COPY . .` copies what was sent. The route-manifest gate
# (backend/tests/test_route_manifest_net_seat.py) reads this file with the same
# rules: a path matched here is out of the image and out of the digest alike,
# and every path NOT matched must be a committed file with its committed bytes,
# or the gate refuses to take a digest at all. Docker reads a line starting
# with # as a comment, so each reason sits on the line above its pattern.

# Bytecode caches: derived from the sources, written by any local run or test.
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo

# Test artefacts.
**/.pytest_cache
**/.coverage
**/htmlcov

# Local virtual environments.
.venv
venv
**/.venv

# Logs and database dumps.
**/*.log
logs
db-backups

# Configuration values and key material: delivered to the container by the
# compose file's environment and mounts, never baked into the image.
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.key
**/*.pem

# The renderer's font binaries: the build fetches each one from its pinned URL
# and verifies it against assets/fonts/fonts.lock.json, and verifies them again
# after the code copy; a font from a checkout must never reach the image.
assets/fonts/*.ttf
assets/fonts/*.otf
assets/fonts/*.ttc
assets/fonts/*.part

# The private card-art staging directory: the running container mounts the
# private bundle read-only at this path.
assets/pc/cards

# Written by the build itself (build_manifest.py), after the copy.
build-manifest.json
